{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidingEndomorphism","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidingEndomorphism","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeDihedralBraidReduction","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.End","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Pi"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_braid_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_braid_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidingEndomorphism.lean#L178-L190","doc":"**Packaged `braid_adjacent` field content** (coset-conditional): for an\nadjacent index pair `(i, i+1)` whose braiding generators are the induced\ndescent structures of a `DihedralCosetStructure`, the family satisfies\n`σ i * σ (i+1) * σ i = σ (i+1) * σ i * σ (i+1)` — the\n`HeckeBraidedPresentation.braid_adjacent` field, conditional on the adjacent\npair carrying the coset datum (the open combinatorial input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_hecke_quadratic_field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_hecke_quadratic_field","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidingEndomorphism.lean#L166-L174","doc":"**Packaged `hecke_quadratic` field content** (unconditional, every rank):\nfor `h = q − q⁻¹`, the endomorphism family `i ↦ braidingEnd (D i) (q − q⁻¹)`\nsatisfies `σ i * σ i = (q − q⁻¹) • σ i + 1` — literally the\n`HeckeBraidedPresentation.hecke_quadratic` field with `H := Module.End F (W → F)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_braid_h3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_braid_h3","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidingEndomorphism.lean#L143-L151","doc":"**n = 3 braid slice** (proved, unconditional): the two concrete H₃ braiding\ngenerators satisfy `σ₀ * σ₁ * σ₀ = σ₁ * σ₀ * σ₁` in `Module.End R (Fin 6 → R)`.\nDischarged directly by the proved n = 3 cell braid `cell_braid` (the transport\nof `H3.braid_operator`), so no coset datum is needed at this concrete rung. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_quadratic_h3σ₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_quadratic_h3σ₁","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidingEndomorphism.lean#L138-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_quadratic_h3σ₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_quadratic_h3σ₀","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidingEndomorphism.lean#L131-L136","doc":"**n = 3 quadratic slices** (proved): both H₃ braiding generators satisfy\nthe Hecke quadratic in `Module.End`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_quadratic_h2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_quadratic_h2","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidingEndomorphism.lean#L122-L129","doc":"**n = 2 quadratic slice** (proved): the single H₂ braiding endomorphism\nsatisfies the Hecke quadratic as a `Module.End` ring identity. The\nendomorphism-framework analogue of the scaffold's diagonal-matrix slice\n`heckeQuadratic_h2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.descentH2σ₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.descentH2σ₀","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidingEndomorphism.lean#L114-L120","doc":"The rank-one (S₂ / H₂) descent structure: step = the transposition `0↔1`,\nlengths `[0,1]`. The single-generator base of the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_braid","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidingEndomorphism.lean#L99-L110","doc":"**The braid relation as a `Module.End` ring identity, at general rank.**\nGiven a `DihedralCosetStructure` on the adjacent pair, the two induced braiding\nendomorphisms satisfy `σᵢ * σⱼ * σᵢ = σⱼ * σᵢ * σⱼ` in `Module.End R (W → R)` —\nthe ring-element form of `braid_of_dihedral` (which reduces the general braid\nto the proved n = 3 cell braid). Coset-conditional exactly as\n`braid_of_dihedral`: the datum's existence for every adjacent pair is the\nisolated open combinatorial input, NOT proved here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidingEndomorphism.lean#L87-L95","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic as a `Module.End` ring identity, at every rank.**\n`braidingEnd D h * braidingEnd D h = h • braidingEnd D h + 1`, where `*` is\ncomposition in `Module.End R (W → R)` and `1` is the identity endomorphism.\nThis is the ring-element form of `mulStep_quadratic` — the exact shape of the\n`HeckeBraidedPresentation.hecke_quadratic` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd_apply","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidingEndomorphism.lean#L82-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.braidingEnd","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidingEndomorphism.lean#L70-L80","doc":"**The braiding morphism `σ` as an honest `R`-linear endomorphism.** The\nIwahori–Hecke length-rule action `mulStep D h` (proved additive and\n`R`-homogeneous) packaged as an element of the endomorphism ring\n`Module.End R (W → R)`. This is the object the `HeckeBraidedPresentation` class\nlives on: composition in `Module.End` is the ring multiplication in which the\nF2 relations below are genuine ring identities. ","signatureChunk":0}]}